WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
There is currently an ongoing court case regarding President Trump's media ban, so let's talk

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.720
about what's going on, why it matters, and why it should concern anyone who cares about

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.720
press freedom.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.880
On Friday, September 18th, President Trump banned CNN, MSNOW, and Politico, all well-known

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.080
left-leaning news sources, from having press access to the White House.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.000
Trump has accused these outlets of spreading fake news, and has gone as far as to say that

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.440
their reporting poses a threat to national security.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.240
Three news outlets have since gone forward with suing the Trump administration, arguing

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.680
that the ban is infringement upon their First Amendment rights.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.880
Nevertheless, the President and his close-ups have doubled down.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.200
A press release published by the White House wrote that, quote,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.920
the First Amendment protects their right to publish.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.760
It does not entitle them to a hard pass,

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.630
briefing room seat, or place in the press pool.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.310
And this is true, the White House does have the ability

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.630
to control press access, but the controversy is over

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:43.110
whether it can selectively exclude news organizations

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.230
because of their reporting and political views.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:46.830
So the claim is that access to the White House

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:47.830
is a privilege and not a right,

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.630
but the doors are only being opened to people

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.470
that agree with the current administration.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:52.630
That is dangerous.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.190
Though this ban is being legally defended

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:55.590
as a way to protect security

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.170
and prevent misinformation from being widespread,

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.330
the claims are super weak,

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.370
and it is clear that it's just being used as a way

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.050
to protect President Trump's image within the media.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:04.930
At one thing to be clear,

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.570
President Trump and his administration

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.090
are not concerned with protecting truth.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.050
When you look at fact checks

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.810
of Trump's own speeches and statements,

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.910
he directly spews lies in a way that is far more direct

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.610
and far more extreme than most news channels in general,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.450
especially the ones being currently banned.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:20.490
I'm not gonna sit here and claim

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:22.650
that left-leaning news is unbiased and all perfect,

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.430
but the issue of misinformation in the media

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.830
is one that spreads across the political spectrum,

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.070
and President Trump is only highlighting it on the left

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.670
because it goes against him.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.030
This is not something to be overlooked.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:33.910
Powerful leaders trying to control the press

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:36.270
is hardly a new concept from a historical perspective,

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.390
and it is something that has proved to be

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.550
politically dangerous time and time again.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.270
The most recent update came this past Friday,

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.470
September 24th, when a US district judge

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.430
ordered a 14-day temporary restraining order against the ban.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:48.270
This ruling was promising, but only temporary,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.070
and the lawsuit is yet to be concluded.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:51.190
Regardless of the final verdict,

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:52.790
this case is super important to pay attention to

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:55.910
Because the fact that a presidential administration is even challenging

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:59.790
freedom of the press like this in itself is a danger to American democracy.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:02.070
Freedom of the press isn't just important, it's fundamental.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.150
So make sure you keep paying attention to what's happening and

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.190
you vote in the midterms.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:05.910
That's all she wrote.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.840
Bye, guys.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.400
Last week, President Trump enacted a very controversial media ban.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.320
So let's talk about what happened, why it matters, and

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.400
why it should concern anyone who cares about press freedom.
